{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1158090-odd-things-little-places-of-power","id":1158090,"title":"[Odd Things] Little Places of Power","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-12T22:58:54-08:00","id":1158090,"title":"[Odd Things] Little Places of Power","content":"There is so much <i>rust</i> on my fingers. I need to shake it off - feel free to join in.<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Suicide Well</b></span><br /> There's an old well up in the woods. If you don't know what you're looking for, you'll miss it - it's little more than a hole in the ground at this point, with a little pail on a rusty chain lying next to it. If you dip that pail in the brackish water, and you drink it down (it's salty and nasty tasting, but it's otherwise clean - you won't vomit unless you have a particularly strong gag reflex.) By the time you get back to town, your greatest wish will come true. Or, well, that's the <i>story</i>, anyway - most everyone who goes up there ends up dead within a month or two. Think you can break the trend?<br /> <br /> <u><i>Systems</i>:</u> The Suicide Well is damn simple. Drinking the water instantly resolves one of your Aspirations - it tends to go for <i>fulfilling</i> Aspirations before any others (if you want a new car and for that rat bastard Carl to kick the bucket, it'll give you the car. If you want Susie Q to fall in love with you, it'll happen). On top of that, Aspirations whose end results are largely impersonal (like finding a cure for cancer) have their effects restricted to be more immediate (you get a cure for <i>your sister's</i> cancer).<br /> <br /> However, there is a price - the Aspiration that replaces the one that was &quot;granted&quot; is always &quot;Die&quot;. As a side effect, you <i>can</i> suffer the Broken Down tilt when someone you're fighting decides to Go For Blood. Drinking from the well only works once for a given person.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Back Room</b></span><br /> Hey, a piece of advice for you - if the barkeep ever offers to let you into the private room in the back, politely decline. I've seen it do <i>nasty</i> things to folks - turns their heads inside-out. It's hard to explain, just... just don't go <i>back</i> there.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Systems</u></i><u>:</u> The back room of the bar is mostly harmless by itself. It's what happens when cigarette smoke fills it up and the brandy gets poured that should get you worried. Anyone who spends an hour back there leaves with the Soulless condition. What's weirder, it directly flips their Vice and Virtue - if your Virtue was Diligent and your Vice was Ambitious, now your Virtue is Ambitious and your Vice is Diligent. If you've got extras due to being Vice-Ridden or Virtuous, flip those around too.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, though - breathing in that smoke leaves its own mark. If you ever fail a Breaking Point roll inside the room, you're hooked. You gain Addicted (Nicotine) as a Persistent Condition instead of the normal condition you'd get - if you dramatically fail the roll, you're immediately Deprived. If you become a Thrall... the smoky air of bar turns off Broken while you're there, and <i>only</i> while you're there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:18:53-08:00","id":1159220,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Wrathful Willow</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'd stay away from that apple grove if I were you. You know the one, way past the Old Miller's place, with the... willow tree. You can't miss it, a willow tree sitting smack dab in the middle of a grove for apples. Nobody's got a clue why the Miller's let it grow in place of one of their red delicious trees, but there it stands. The bark's got knots and claw marks all around, like someone's taken their anger out on it, but the tree as a whole seems healthier than ever. The trees around it too, they spit out more apples than a dozen people could eat, and all those shiny red delicious sit and rot on the earth, where they belong.</span><br /> <br /> <u><i>System:</i></u><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The grove might look innocuous, but it's a place of power; angry, bloody, murderous power. Anybody who eats an apple from this orchard replaces their Vice with Wrathful, and immediately gains a Berserk Condition for mortals and mages, and activates any supernatural form of rage/frenzy that your splat has, Blood Frenzy for Vampires, Demonic Rage for Demons, etc etc.</span><br /> <br /> It comes with a benefit, however: anyone who eats the apple must roll for a Breaking Point, and if they succeed, will actually regain 2 points of their Integrity/Wisdom/Humanity/etc etc. This Breaking Point roll can be made at any point once 3 turns of the Frenzy have occurred, with failure making the Frenzy last until the end of the scene, the player is knocked out, or manages to regain control through a Composure+Intelligence roll. The apples in this orchard only work once per character, and will always leave visitors a little more temperamental than when they left.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Charlie's Jukebox</b></span><br /> We've all seen Charlie's, wedged between two office buildings, right on the corner of MLK Blvd and Providence Ave, though I'm not sure anybody'd call that place a working of God. The place only has two employees, Charlie and Dennis. Charlie cooks, Dennis waits. The place has a 50s vibe and looks taken care of, though you'll never see Dennis cleaning anything other than the countertop. Dennis and Charlie look like two well-groomed thirty-something year olds and are some of the nicest staff you'll ever meet, but there's one thing in that place that'll keep me out for years. The Jukebox over in the corner, which Charlie said's been there since his dad, Charlie Sr, ran the place, does weird stuff to people, makes em do weird things, things normal people just don't do.<br /> <br /> <u><i>System:</i></u> Charlie's Jukebox looks like every other 50s-esque jukebox, neon lights, wood paneling, but when you put the quarter in and pick a song, you gain a random persistent Condition based on what song is played (Player picks, ST decides Condition that fits). As payment for indulging the Jukebox's madness, one of your Aspirations are immediately fulfilled, picked at random, and replaced with 'Cure &lt;condition&gt;'. This Aspiration does not give anything upon completion.<br /> <br /> Charlie and Dennis don't seem any different from baseline mortals, but they never go near the Jukebox, and since the booths are arranged so the Jukebox is almost alone, Dennis doesn't have to walk by it to deliver plates of food. He won't talk about it when asked either, directing all questions to Charlie, who usually just shrugs and mentions it was his dad's and leaves it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","name":"PrinceVertigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}